From: William Horvath <william@horvath.blog>
Subject: [PATCH] main: Fix quitting from SDL_EVENT_TERMINATING on Emscripten

Since SDL_MainCallbacksSawEventTerminating, the Emscripten beforeunload handler
calls SDL_QuitMainCallbacks() from inside the event watcher dispatch, so
SDL_Quit() frees the watcher list while SDL_DispatchEventWatchList is still
walking it ("null function" on the next watcher). The main loop also kept
running, so its next iteration called SDL_AppQuit() a second time with a NULL
appstate.
---
--- a/src/events/SDL_eventwatch.c
+++ b/src/events/SDL_eventwatch.c
@@ -58,7 +58,8 @@
         }
 
         list->dispatching = true;
-        for (i = 0; i < count; ++i) {
+        // a watcher can shut down the event subsystem (SDL_EVENT_TERMINATING quits the app on some platforms), freeing the list
+        for (i = 0; i < count && list->watchers; ++i) {
             if (!list->watchers[i].removed) {
                 list->watchers[i].callback(list->watchers[i].userdata, event);
             }
--- a/src/main/emscripten/SDL_sysmain_callbacks.c
+++ b/src/main/emscripten/SDL_sysmain_callbacks.c
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@
 {
     // We leave `result` alone, so if SDL_AppEvent didn't set something else, SDL_APP_CONTINUE will signify the app is terminating in an unexpected way during SDL_AppQuit.
     const SDL_AppResult result = (SDL_AppResult) SDL_GetAtomicInt(apprc);
+    emscripten_cancel_main_loop();  // otherwise its next iteration would see the result and quit again.
     SDL_QuitMainCallbacks(result);  // we need to call this directly because we won't be returning to where this would be called later.
 }
 
